.env
data/
.venv
node_modules
dist/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
config.local.json
# ...and any editor/backup spinoff of it: the base name is ignored but
# `config.local.json.bak` etc. are NOT, so a `git add -A` could commit personal
# paths and credentials. Same trap for .env.
config.local.json.*
# The one sanctioned exception, same pattern as .env.example below: a COMMITTED
# synthetic template (docs/CONFIG.md documents it; secret-scan guards its
# content). Spinoffs like config.local.json.bak stay ignored.
!config.local.json.example
.env.*
!.env.example
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
# The personal-content deny-list for scripts/secret-scan.sh. It names real
# people, places, and projects, so it is personal data in its own right and
# must never be committed. Committed template: secret-scan-local.example.
.secret-scan-local
